{
  "id": "spastic-dysarthria",
  "term": "spastic dysarthria",
  "definition": "Spastic dysarthria is an acquired speech disorder caused by neurological injury in which muscle control for speech becomes tense, slow, imprecise, or poorly coordinated, reducing how understandable speech is. It can affect breathing, voice production, resonance, and speech rhythm, often leading to slow, effortful speech, unclear pronunciation, and hypernasality, with social and emotional impact.",
